+# Spec — task_027: dotted-repo-name detection fix + brain2 vibe-operation note
+
+## Task summary
+
+Two defects surfaced 2026-07-21 by a real session (andeye_com). (A) `detect_github_repo`'s regex pins the repo segment to `[^/.]+`, so a repo whose NAME contains dots (`andeyePro/andeye.com`) never parses — vibe wrongly claims "No GitHub repo found" and offers to create a new repo, on every launch. (B) In-container Claudes know nothing about the host-side vibe CLI, so when a launcher issue appears they guess (that session invented a nonexistent "path registry") or punt ("run `vibe --help` yourself"). Fix: (A) parse `owner/repo` allowing dots, stripping `.git` in shell; (B) the launcher maintains an auto-refreshed `vibe --help` note in the user's brain2 (`<brain2>/meta/vibe-operation.md`), and a new shipped CLAUDE.md fragment points in-container Claudes at it with a give-exact-commands discipline.
+
+## Pinned contract
+
+### A — `detect_github_repo`
+
+- New algorithm, replacing the current single regex: take `url=$(git remote get-url origin)` as today; strip ONE trailing `/` (`url="${url%/}"`); match `[[ "$url" =~ github\.com[:/]([^/]+/[^/]+)$ ]]`; let `slug="${BASH_REMATCH[1]}"`; strip ONE trailing `.git` (`slug="${slug%.git}"`); return the slug (echo, rc 0) ONLY if `is_valid_repo_slug "$slug"` passes; otherwise return 1. No other behaviour change; non-github and no-remote still return 1.
+- Consequences pinned as correct and unchanged: `save_token`/`lookup_token` key literally (dots fine); credential-helper `_sanitise_slug` maps non-alphanumerics to `_` (dots fine); a repo literally named `foo.git` arrives as `foo.git.git` in the URL and resolves to `foo.git` (single strip — never a loop).
+
+### B — brain2 ops note + fragment
+
+- New sourceable launcher function `refresh_brain2_vibe_note`, ALWAYS returns 0 — and the fail-soft mechanism is pinned, not just the outcome (an unguarded write into an unwritable dir under `set -euo pipefail` kills the whole sourced shell): EVERY filesystem operation in the function is individually errexit-guarded with stderr silenced — `mkdir -p "$p/meta" 2>/dev/null || return 0`; `[ -w "$p/meta" ] || return 0`; content written to a temp file then moved, each step `2>/dev/null || return 0` (or the equivalent `if !` form). Belt-and-braces: the launch-path call site is written `refresh_brain2_vibe_note || true` (same call-context errexit suppression the task_026 `setup_token` fix pinned). Resolve `p=$(_brain2_source)`; return 0 silently when empty (covers `VIBE_BRAIN2_PATH=off`) or when `$p` is not an existing directory (never create the brain2 root; mirrors the mount-gating rule). Otherwise the guarded `mkdir -p "$p/meta"`; target file `$p/meta/vibe-operation.md`, created with the single heading line `# vibe — CLI operation (auto-maintained)` if absent. Maintain a managed block at the END of the file, markers exactly `<!-- >>> vibe-cli-help (auto, do not edit) >>>` and `<!-- <<< vibe-cli-help <<< -->` (distinct from existing vibe markers); strip-and-reappend using the same awk idiom as `install_claude_md_fragments` (preserve ALL content outside the markers; trim trailing blank lines; idempotent — two consecutive runs leave one block, byte-identical). Block body: a line `Generated by vibe <version> at <UTC ISO8601>` (version via `_vibe_version`; timestamp via `date -u`), then the full `vibe --help` text inside a ```text fence. Capture mechanism (sourcing-safe — `usage()` greps `"$0"`, which is `bash` when vibe is sourced by a smoke test, so calling it is FORBIDDEN here): factor a new `_usage_text()` holding usage()'s two emission steps but grepping `"$VIBE_REPO_DIR/vibe"` (BASH_SOURCE-derived, sourcing-safe) instead of `"$0"`, with no `exit`; `usage()` becomes exactly `_usage_text` + `exit 0` (help output byte-identical); the note writer captures `help_text=$(_usage_text)`.
+- Call site: one guarded line in the launch path (host-side, before container launch, after config/token setup — placement flexible within that window), unconditional per launch. Subcommand paths (`pat`, `learn`, `repos`, `audit`, `--help`) do NOT refresh the note.
+- New fragment `devcontainer/claude-md/vibe-cli.md` (auto-collected by the existing sorted-glob sync in `install_claude_md_fragments` — no manifest edit exists or is needed). Content requirements (prose, concise, in the style of sibling fragments): for host-side vibe launcher matters (PAT setup/rotation, repo detection/registration, rebuilds, flags), the source of truth is `/brain2/meta/vibe-operation.md` when mounted — it holds the CURRENT installed `vibe --help`, refreshed every launch; if brain2 is not mounted, ask the user to type `! vibe --help` so the output lands in the conversation; ALWAYS answer with the exact command to run and state which side (Mac host vs container) it runs on; NEVER answer with "go find the right command yourself" or equivalent. Must contain the literal strings `vibe-operation.md`, `! vibe --help`, and `exact command`; plus one line noting that prose OUTSIDE the note's managed block is ordinary brain2 content under the normal brain2 trust discipline (only the managed block is machine-generated).
+
+## Files in scope
+
+- `vibe` — `detect_github_repo` rewrite; `refresh_brain2_vibe_note`; its one-line call site.
+- `devcontainer/claude-md/vibe-cli.md` — new fragment.
+- `README.md` — one short addition in the brain2 section: the auto-refreshed `meta/vibe-operation.md` ops note (must contain `vibe-operation.md`).
+- `MANUAL-TESTS.md` — one new entry: real-launch verification that the note appears/refreshes in a configured brain2, and that a dotted-name repo (andeye_com) now detects (must contain `vibe-operation.md`).
+- `TODO.md` + `CHANGELOG.md` — per repo convention, same commit.
+- NOT in scope for Generator: `smoke-test.py` `test_task027_*` functions (Tester-owned; cycle-anchored freeze).
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+All host-side, no docker/network; sourced-function convention with tmp `$HOME`/tmp dirs; `set +e; …; set -e` bracketing for calls expected to return non-zero (sourced vibe carries `set -euo pipefail`).
+
+1. `detect_github_repo` in a tmp git repo returns, per origin URL: `https://github.com/andeyePro/andeye.com.git` → `andeyePro/andeye.com`; `https://github.com/andeyePro/andeye.com` → same; `git@github.com:owner/repo.git` → `owner/repo`; `ssh://git@github.com/owner/repo.git` → `owner/repo`; `https://github.com/owner/repo.git` → `owner/repo` (regression); `https://github.com/owner/repo/` (trailing slash) → `owner/repo`; `https://github.com/owner/foo.git.git` → `foo.git` repo segment.
+2. `detect_github_repo` returns rc 1 (no output) for: no remote; a non-github remote (`https://gitlab.com/o/r.git`); a github URL whose slug fails `is_valid_repo_slug` (e.g. embedded `%20` or `$`).
+3. `refresh_brain2_vibe_note` with a tmp brain2 dir: creates `meta/vibe-operation.md` containing the heading, both exact markers, the `Generated by vibe ` line, and real help content (assert the literal strings `Usage:` — from the help text — and `vibe pat`), and returns 0.
+4. Re-run idempotence: pre-seed the file with user prose above the block AND run the function twice — user prose intact, exactly ONE open marker and ONE close marker, function returns 0 each time.
+5. Fail-soft gating: `VIBE_BRAIN2_PATH=off` → no file created, rc 0; `VIBE_BRAIN2_PATH` pointing at a nonexistent dir → no dir created, rc 0; an existing brain2 dir with an UNWRITABLE `meta/` (chmod 500) → rc still 0, no abort under `set -euo pipefail`.
+6. Launch-path wiring, anchor-pinned static check: the `refresh_brain2_vibe_note || true` call line appears BETWEEN the line matching `# ── GitHub setup` and the line matching `# ── Build the image` in `vibe`, and nowhere else in the file except its own definition.
+7. `devcontainer/claude-md/vibe-cli.md` exists and contains `vibe-operation.md`, `! vibe --help`, and `exact command`; and the string `vibe-cli` does NOT appear in `devcontainer/install-claude-extras.sh` (the fragment collection is a sorted directory glob with named special-cases like `ssh-discipline` — absence proves `vibe-cli.md` rides the glob unconditionally, no manifest edit).
+8. `python3 code-check.py` passes; every pre-existing test function (everything except new `test_task027_*` additions), unchanged, still passes — full-suite run (regression gate; NEVER spawned from within smoke-test.py itself).
+9. `README.md` contains `vibe-operation.md`; `MANUAL-TESTS.md` contains `vibe-operation.md`.
+10. No token/secret material in any new output: the note writer emits nothing to stdout/stderr on success, and the note content is help text only (assert the fixture-free note contains no `ghp_` substring).
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Migrating/renaming any existing brain2 note content (the managed block append preserves whatever is there).
+- Writing per-repo copies of the help text into project workspaces or containers.
+- Any in-container writer for the note (host launcher only).
+- Registry/rename handling beyond the regex fix (there is no path registry; none is added).
+- Changing `_brain2_source` or `install_claude_md_fragments`. (`usage()` may ONLY be reshaped into the pinned `_usage_text` + `exit 0` form — output byte-identical.)
+
+## Test location
+
+`smoke-test.py` — Tester appends `test_task027_*` functions. Cycle-anchored freeze: once committed, frozen for this task; Generator never edits them.
+
+## Proposed budget
+
+3 cycles — two independent small features, both with strong in-repo precedent (regex helpers, managed-block writers).
+
+## Model plan
+
+- Generator: sonnet, ceiling opus. Difficulty: low-medium (regex edge cases + block-management idiom, both with precedent).
+- Tester: haiku (new task resets to defaults per harness rule — task_026's quality escalation does not carry over), escalating per ladder. Spec Critic: sonnet. Chair: session model (Fable 5).
+- Fable rung: not pre-authorised.
