+- [x] **task_027: dotted-repo-name detection fix + auto-refreshed brain2 `vibe-operation.md` note** — two defects surfaced 2026-07-21 by a real session (andeye_com). (A) `detect_github_repo`'s old regex pinned the repo segment to `[^/.]+`, so a repo whose NAME contains a dot (`andeyePro/andeye.com`) never parsed — vibe wrongly reported "No GitHub repo found" and offered to create a new one, on every launch. New algorithm: take `git remote get-url origin` as before; strip ONE trailing `/`; match `github\.com[:/]([^/]+/[^/]+)$` (dots now allowed in both segments, greedy to end-of-string); strip ONE trailing `.git` in shell (never a loop — a repo literally named `foo.git` arrives as `foo.git.git` in the URL and correctly resolves back to `foo.git`, not `foo`); gate the result through the existing `is_valid_repo_slug` before returning, so a github.com-shaped but malformed slug (`%20`, `$`, etc.) still fails rather than reaching callers. Non-github and no-remote cases return 1 unchanged; `save_token`/`lookup_token`/credential-helper `_sanitise_slug` were already dot-safe, no changes needed there. (B) in-container Claudes have no visibility into the host-side vibe CLI, so a launcher question got guessed at (a prior session invented a nonexistent "path registry") or punted ("run `vibe --help` yourself"). New sourceable `refresh_brain2_vibe_note`, called unconditionally in the launch path (`refresh_brain2_vibe_note || true`, between the `# ── GitHub setup` and `# ── Build the image` anchors — task_026's call-context errexit-suppression discipline) auto-maintains a managed block at the end of `<brain2>/meta/vibe-operation.md` holding the CURRENT `vibe --help` text plus a `Generated by vibe <version> at <UTC ISO8601>` line, refreshed every launch; strip-and-reappend uses the same awk idiom as `install_claude_md_fragments` (distinct markers — `vibe-cli-help`, not `vibe-managed` — since it's a different file with a different lifecycle), so hand-written brain2 prose above the block survives untouched and two consecutive runs leave exactly one block. ALWAYS returns 0: every filesystem operation inside is individually guarded (`mkdir -p ... 2>/dev/null || return 0`, `[ -w ... ] || return 0`, temp-file-then-`mv`, each `2>/dev/null || return 0`) so an unwritable `meta/` under `set -euo pipefail` degrades silently rather than aborting the whole sourced launcher — verified directly with a `chmod 500` fixture. Never creates the brain2 root itself (mirrors the existing mount-gating rule); no-ops cleanly on `VIBE_BRAIN2_PATH=off` or a nonexistent brain2 dir. The capture is sourcing-safe: `usage()`'s old `grep '^#' "$0"` breaks when vibe is sourced (`$0` is `bash`, not the vibe script, under smoke-test.py's `VIBE_SOURCE_ONLY=1` convention or this note-writer's own invocation) — factored into `_usage_text()`, which greps `"$VIBE_REPO_DIR/vibe"` (BASH_SOURCE-derived) instead and has no `exit`; `usage()` is now exactly `_usage_text` + `exit 0`, help output byte-identical. New fragment `devcontainer/claude-md/vibe-cli.md` (rides the existing sorted-glob fragment sync unconditionally — `vibe-cli` does not appear in `install-claude-extras.sh`, no manifest edit) tells in-container Claudes to treat `/brain2/meta/vibe-operation.md`'s managed block as ground truth when mounted, to ask for `! vibe --help` pasted into the conversation when it isn't, and to always answer with the exact command and which side (host vs container) it runs on rather than punting. README's brain2 section and a new MANUAL-TESTS Test 38 (dotted-name regression, note creation/idempotence/version-bump, brain2-off no-op, and the in-container "reads the note instead of guessing" behaviour) document the feature; `smoke-test.py` `test_task027_*` coverage is Tester-owned for this cycle. TDD: a scratch harness (not committed — gitignored under `.vs/cycle-1/scratch-tests/`) drove the full AC1/AC2 regex table (all seven URL forms plus the four rejection cases), the sourcing-safe `_usage_text` capture (byte-identical to `vibe --help` stdout), and `refresh_brain2_vibe_note`'s idempotence (exact-line marker counts, not substring) and chmod-500 fail-soft survival — including invoking the real call-site pattern (`refresh_brain2_vibe_note || true` under a bare `set -euo pipefail` subshell) to prove the launcher itself survives, not just the function in isolation — all green (39/39). Verified: `python3 code-check.py` clean; full pre-existing `python3 smoke-test.py` green, no regressions.
