 - [x] **task_026: `vibe pat [owner/repo]` PAT rotation + launch-time 401 auto-reprompt** — vibe had no rotation path: `setup_token` only fires when NO token is stored, so an expired/revoked fine-grained PAT meant hand-editing `~/.vibe/tokens`. Adds a host-side `vibe pat [owner/repo]` subcommand, dispatched (and exits) before `parse_vibe_args`, same convention as `learn`/`repos`/`audit`: no arg infers the repo via `detect_github_repo` (stderr hint + exit 1 on failure); an explicit slug is validated with the existing `is_valid_repo_slug` (one `/`, `[A-Za-z0-9._-]+` both sides); `--help`/`-h` prints usage and exits 0 BEFORE slug validation; any other arg count is a one-line stderr usage error, exit 1. Core `rotate_token <repo>` prints `Repo: <owner/repo>` then `stored token found — it will be replaced` / `no stored token yet`, then the settings-tokens URL (never auto-opens a browser), then reads the new token via an errexit-guarded `read -rsp` (same `_learning_capture` idiom, vibe ~1438 — immediate EOF can't abort `set -e` before the abort message prints); empty input (EOF or a lone newline) aborts with `aborted — token store unchanged` on stderr, store byte-identical; non-empty overwrites via the existing `save_token` and confirms with `✓ Token saved for <repo>. Takes effect on the next vibe launch (no rebuild needed).` — never prints the token itself. Launch-time half: `stored_token_rejected <repo> <token>` makes one `curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' --max-time 5 -K -` call per launch, feeding `header = "Authorization: Bearer <token>"` via a here-string so the token never touches curl's argv (`ps`-visible) or disk; curl's own exit status is ignored entirely — only an exact `401` returns rejected, every other outcome (200/403/404/5xx/000/curl failure/empty) fails open. Wrapper `maybe_reprompt_stored_token <repo> <token>` (sourceable, unit-testable) no-ops when `VIBE_PAT_CHECK=0` or the token is empty, otherwise probes and — only on rejection — prints `  ⚠ Stored PAT for <repo> was rejected by GitHub (expired or revoked) — let's replace it.` and re-runs the existing `setup_token` flow; it ALWAYS returns 0 regardless of branch, since its one-line call site (`GITHUB_TOKEN=$(lookup_token ...)`'s non-empty/else branch, vibe ~2768) sits under `set -euo pipefail` and any other return would turn a healthy launch into a hard failure. `vibe --help` gains the `vibe pat` line plus a `HOST shell` caveat, matching the `vibe learn` block's style. README's token-store row and a new MANUAL-TESTS Test 37 (manual rotation, end-to-end revoked-PAT reprompt, `VIBE_PAT_CHECK=0` suppression — needs live GitHub) document the feature; `smoke-test.py` `test_task026_*` coverage is Tester-owned for this cycle. TDD: a scratch harness (not committed — gitignored under `.vs/cycle-1/scratch-tests/`) drove all ten ACs red-then-green, including the curl-shim argv/stdin capture (proves the fixture token never reaches argv) and a placement-aware static check that the launch-path call sits inside the stored-token `else` branch, not the fresh-paste one. Verified: `python3 code-check.py` clean (19 files); full pre-existing `python3 smoke-test.py` green, no regressions. Cycle 2 (security-review gate, three findings fixed): the wrapper's `setup_token` call is now `|| true`-guarded — a rejected token on a NON-interactive launch (stdin closed: cron/scripted `vibe`) previously hit `setup_token`'s unguarded `read`, whose EOF status hard-aborted the whole launcher under `set -euo pipefail`, exactly the block-the-launch outcome the fail-open contract forbids (reproduced red, then green); `detect_github_repo`'s looser-than-`is_valid_repo_slug` output is now validated at both new sinks (the wrapper fails open, `vibe pat`'s no-arg path refuses loudly); and `rotate_token` rejects pasted tokens containing `"`/`\`/whitespace/control chars before they can reach the curl `-K` config line. Frozen-test additions `test_task026_c2_*` cover all three, including the real-`setup_token` closed-stdin survival case the cycle-1 stubs couldn't see. Final suite: 1823 checks green.
